1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,132
We're SARcastic Scientists from Islamabad.

2
00:00:03,172 --> 00:00:06,370
This is SARtale, for Dancing with the SARs.

3
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:10,766
In 2022, the Shisper glacial lake burst and swept away the

4
00:00:10,806 --> 00:00:12,726
Karakoram Highway bridge.

5
00:00:12,766 --> 00:00:16,519
These lakes fill in summer, when cloud hides them from

6
00:00:16,559 --> 00:00:18,100
optical satellites.

7
00:00:18,490 --> 00:00:20,100
Here is Attabad:

8
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:24,750
seventy percent cloud in the optical image, but clear in

9
00:00:24,790 --> 00:00:27,600
NISAR radar, from NASA and ISRO.

10
00:00:27,990 --> 00:00:32,536
For every pass, SARtale measures each lake's water against

11
00:00:32,576 --> 00:00:36,405
its own normal range and gives one plain status.

12
00:00:36,445 --> 00:00:38,770
Frozen lakes are set aside.

13
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:43,587
Lake Watch covers thirty-nine lakes in Gilgit-Baltistan and

14
00:00:43,627 --> 00:00:45,306
Khyber Pakhtunkhwa.

15
00:00:45,346 --> 00:00:49,842
Each lake's page says what changed, how sure we are, and who

16
00:00:49,882 --> 00:00:51,010
to contact.

17
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:55,607
It refreshes every week, and anyone can request a new lake.

18
00:00:55,647 --> 00:00:58,090
Open source, built on NASA data.
